\title{A counterexample in quasi-category theory}
\author/literal{Alexander Campbell}
\meta{venue}{[[pams]]}
\meta{doi}{10.1090/proc/14692}
\meta{arxiv}{1904.04965}

\subtree{
\taxon{Abstract}
\p{
We give an example of a morphism of simplicial sets which is a monomorphism,
bijective on 0-simplices, and a weak categorical equivalence, but which is not inner
anodyne. This answers an open question of [Joyal](andrejoyal). Furthermore, we use
this morphism to refute a plausible description of the class of fibrations in
[Joyal](andrejoyal)'s model structure for quasi-categories.
}
}

